axiom> help
commands:
  help                  this list
  echo <text>           print text
  date                  wall clock (RTC-anchored, no time zone)
  uptime                time since boot (TSC)
  clocks                compare the PIT, TSC and RTC since boot
  ps                    processes: pid, parent, state, rights, name
  rights                this shell's rights
  run <program> [+evidence] [+read] [-send]
                        start a boot module (or a file: /path) and wait; it gets
                        SEND by default, +evidence adds EVIDENCE, +read READ,
                        -send removes SEND
  ls                    files: size, version, SHA-256 prefix, name
  cat <file>            print a file (hash-verified by the kernel)
  write <file> <text>   create or replace a file with text
  rm <file>             delete a file
  install <module> <file>  copy a boot module into the file system
  df                    file-system root hash, generation, space, mode
  ledger                verify the newest evidence records' hash chain
  lat [reset]           kernel interrupts-off times and tick gaps (reset: clear)
  exit                  leave (the kernel starts a new shell)
